\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u\\,(\\pi \\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139533501 17592186405019 true] [17592186405161 1071 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ at the point $(0,0,2),$ with parameter $t=0$ at this point." 13194139533501 17592186405019 true] [17592186405161 1071 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ at the point $(0,0,2).$" 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405168 1071 "A tank is being filled with water. The rate of change of the volume of water in the tank $V,$ in milliliters, due to inflow is directly proportional to the time $t,$ measured in hours, with positive constant of proportionality $k$. Additionally, the tank is also leaking $200\\,\\text{ml}$ of water every hour. What is the differential equation that describes the rate of change of the volume of water in the tank, at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time (in hours) since the tank started filling?" 13194139533501 17592186405019 true] [17592186405168 1071 "A tank is being filled with water. The rate of change of the volume of water in the tank $V,$ in milliliters, is directly proportional to the time $t,$ measured in hours. Additionally, the tank is also leaking $200\\,\\text{ml}$ of water every hour. What is the differential equation that describes the rate of change of the volume of water in the tank, at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time (in hours) since the tank started filling?" 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405175 1071 "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\be