n solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+1+12 & =0+1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+12 & =1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x-1)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x-1)^{2}=-11.$ Therefore, circle has no $x$-intercepts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ea/ea1410ea792ac5fb09316bc6d417c2ba46f84c050491b1e351f360eac50deb6c.png)" 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405182 1074 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts.  \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the locus and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2x+6y+12 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{0}^{2}-2x+6\\cdot 0+12 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+1+12 & =0+1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+12 & =1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x-1)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x-1)^{2}=-11.$ Therefore, the locus has no $x$-intercepts." 13194139533501 17592186405019 true] [17592186405183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405184 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405185 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405186 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405187 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405188 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1077 "selection" 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1079 #edb/ref 17592186405184 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405183 1080 #uuid "49673678-7bc5-5316-be28-063bdf75dac5" 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405184 1081 "The circle has no $x$-intercepts" 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045